    {
      "id": "s02",
      "section": "why_midsurface",
      "narration": "To simulate a thin metal part, engineers break it into small mesh blocks. Thin walls need huge numbers of tiny blocks, so simulation runs very slow. Instead, we replace the thin solid with one surface in the middle, called a midsurface. This cuts the number of blocks way down and saves solve time.",
      "budget_s": [
        20,
        25
      ],
      "facts": [],
