    {
      "id": "s04",
      "section": "theory",
      "narration": "Why does the built-in tool break so often? Because it matches opposing pairs of faces across gaps. Our automated method runs in four clear step stages. Step one scans gap distances across faces to vote on wall thickness. The thickness value with the largest total area wins. Step two copies one smooth outer skin and shifts it inward by half that value. Avoiding face pairs means bends never break apart cleanly. Step three repairs holes, ribs, and bends, and it also bridges open seams and dents. Step four checks the finished shell against the original solid volume. Any large area drift gets flagged right away for quick user review.",
      "budget_s": [
        43,
        51
      ],
      "facts": [
        "builtin_method",
        "thickness_vote_example",
        "audit_threshold"
      ],
      "visual": {
